      shortDefinition: 'Investigates being, existence, categories, identity, modality, dependence, and what theories commit us to, while preserving historically different projects that do not share one vocabulary.',
      oneSentencePurpose: 'Asks what there is, what it is to be, and how entities, categories, and levels of reality depend on one another.',
      beginnerExplanation: 'Ontology begins with “what exists?” but does not stop at a list. It asks whether people, properties, numbers, events, processes, possibilities, and institutions exist in the same way; what makes them the kinds they are; and which depend on other things. “Ontology” and “metaphysics” overlap, and their boundary remains disputed.',
